  <lrml:Statements>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="p10-responsibility">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p10-responsibility.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Paragraph 10 and footnote 1 support a continuing responsibility requirement; this rule does not select a discharge test.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Retain ultimate responsibility for management, operational soundness and ownership record keeping regardless of outsourcing.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="p11-records">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p11-records.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Represent the paragraph 11 requirement separately from paragraph 10 sufficiency.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Ensure proper ownership-interest records are maintained and the arrangement is operationally compatible with involved service providers.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="p14-confirmation">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p14-confirmation.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: The inserted request condition attaches to demonstration; confirmation is represented separately.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Confirm management and operational soundness, ownership record keeping and smart-contract integrity to the SFC.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="p14-A-demonstration">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p14-request</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>An applicable SFC request for paragraph 14 demonstration covers the assessed activity and interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p14-A-demonstration.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Reading A takes the express main-text request condition for demonstration; footnote 5's object and standard remain disputed.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Demonstrate to the SFC's satisfaction the paragraph 14 subjects: management and operational soundness, ownership record keeping and smart-contract integrity.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="fn5-B-demonstration">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>fn5-B-demonstration.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Reading B treats the unqualified footnote demonstration wording as standing; the contrary main-text condition is retained.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Demonstrate at least compliance with paragraphs 10–13 and absence of smart-contract vulnerabilities or security flaws with a high level of confidence.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="fn5-C-demonstration">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p14-request</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>An applicable SFC request for paragraph 14 demonstration covers the assessed activity and interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>fn5-C-demonstration.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Reading C attaches footnote minimum content to the main-text request-triggered demonstration.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Demonstrate to the SFC's satisfaction at least compliance with paragraphs 10–13 and absence of smart-contract vulnerabilities or security flaws with a high level of confidence.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="p15-audit">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p15-request</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>An applicable SFC request for paragraph 15 third-party audit or verification covers the assessed activity and interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p15-audit.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Preserve this paragraph's own SFC request, activity and object; a different request does not satisfy it.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Obtain third-party audit or verification on management and operational soundness, ownership record keeping and smart-contract integrity.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="p16-opinion">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>26EC22-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 26EC22 applies to the entity, product, activity and whole assessment interval, with relevant conditions, amendments and relaxations accounted for.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>product-provider</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity has the Product Provider role for this product and activity throughout the assessment interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p16-request</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>An applicable SFC request for paragraph 16 satisfactory legal opinion covers the application and interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>p16-opinion.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Preserve this paragraph's own SFC request, activity and object; a different request does not satisfy it.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Obtain satisfactory legal opinion supporting the application.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="ut68-register">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained UT provision applies to this scheme and actor for the whole assessment interval, including actual conditions and relaxations.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>register-actor</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The entity is the scheme or, for a unit trust, the trustee or person appointed by that trustee to maintain the register.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut68-register.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Preserve the scheme/trustee/appointed-person role disjunction; do not assign every Product Provider this role.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_MUST</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Maintain the register of holders in the specified register-keeper capacity.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="ut68-register-address">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained UT provision applies to this scheme and actor for the whole assessment interval, including actual conditions and relaxations.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>register-actor</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The entity is the scheme or, for a unit trust, the trustee or person appointed by that trustee to maintain the register.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>register-address-request</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The Commission has made an applicable request for the address where this register is kept.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut68-register-address.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Keep the requested register-address disclosure distinct from continuous register maintenance.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_MUST</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Advise the Commission of the address where the register is kept.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="ut611c-selection">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained UT provision applies to this scheme and actor for the whole assessment interval, including actual conditions and relaxations.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>management-company</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity is the management company for this scheme and period.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>valuation-outsourced</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>A third party is engaged in valuation of this scheme's assets within the scope of UT 6.11C.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut611c-selection.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Conditionally render the first sentence's shall as MUST, preserving its valuation-specific actor and activity.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_MUST</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence in selecting, appointing and monitoring the valuation third party, including the stated knowledge, experience and resources criterion.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="ut611c-valuation">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained UT provision applies to this scheme and actor for the whole assessment interval, including actual conditions and relaxations.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>management-company</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity is the management company for this scheme and period.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>valuation-outsourced</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>A third party is engaged in valuation of this scheme's assets within the scope of UT 6.11C.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>ut611c-valuation.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: The second sentence uses should for supervision and review; keep it separate from the first sentence's shall.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Subject the third party's valuation activities to ongoing supervision and periodic review by the management company.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="securities13-responsibility">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>23EC52-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 23EC52 applies in the specified intermediary capacity for the whole interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>intermediary</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity acts as intermediary for the specified activity, product and period.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>issuance-involvement</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The intermediary issues or is substantially involved in issuance of the assessed Tokenised Securities.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>dealing-advising-intent</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The Tokenised Securities at issue are securities which this intermediary intends to deal in or advise on.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>securities13-responsibility.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Retain both issuance involvement and intention to deal in or advise on the specified securities.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_DESCRIPTIVE</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Remain responsible for the overall tokenisation operation notwithstanding outsourcing.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
    <lrml:ConstitutiveStatement key="securities18-controls">
      <ruleml:Rule>
        <ruleml:if>
          <ruleml:And>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>authority-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>23EC52-applicable</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>This retained edition of 23EC52 applies in the specified intermediary capacity for the whole interval.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>intermediary</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessed entity acts as intermediary for the specified activity, product and period.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>securities-distribution-role</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The intermediary deals in, advises on or manages portfolios investing in the assessed Tokenised Securities.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>observed-fact</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>before-activity</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>The assessment concerns controls before commencement of that identified related activity.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Atom>
              <ruleml:Rel>inference-premise</ruleml:Rel>
              <ruleml:Ind>securities18-controls.interpretation</ruleml:Ind>
              <ruleml:Ind>Assume this source-to-rule interpretation, including its stated trigger, object, standard and applicability transfer: Read paragraph 18 within paragraph 17's dealing, advising and portfolio activities.</ruleml:Ind>
            </ruleml:Atom>
          </ruleml:And>
        </ruleml:if>
        <ruleml:then>
          <ruleml:Atom>
            <ruleml:Rel>conditional_SHOULD</ruleml:Rel>
            <ruleml:Ind>Understand and be satisfied with issuer and vendor controls for ownership and technology risks before the related activity.</ruleml:Ind>
          </ruleml:Atom>
        </ruleml:then>
      </ruleml:Rule>
    </lrml:ConstitutiveStatement>
  </lrml:Statements>
</lrml:LegalRuleML>
